


// ...................................... Optimized Solution ......................................

class Solution {
    public ListNode flattenLinkedList(ListNode head) {
        PriorityQueue<ListNode> pq = new PriorityQueue<>((a,b) -> a.val - b.val);
        ListNode temp = head;

        while(temp != null){
            pq.add(temp);
            temp = temp.next;
        }

        ListNode dummy = new ListNode();
        ListNode dummyTemp = dummy;

        while(!pq.isEmpty()){
            ListNode curr = pq.poll();
            dummyTemp.child = curr;
            if(curr.child != null){
                pq.add(curr.child);
            }
            dummyTemp = dummyTemp.child;
        }

        return dummy.child;

    }
}

Time Complexity :- O(M * N) + O(T log(N)) == O(T log (N)) --> T = M * N where N is number of lists and m is total childs in each list

Space Complexity :- O(N) --> priority queue is used for storing N nodes at a time